💥 🔴 Real Failure Scenario
🎯 Issue:
After AKS upgrade:
Pods are running ✅
But application is failing ❌
Errors:
403 Forbidden
Managed Identity authentication failed


🧠 Root Cause (later found)
👉 System-assigned identity lost access / token issues after upgrade
🔍 Step-by-Step Debugging (Real Flow)

✅ Step 1: Check Pods Status
kubectl get pods -A
✔️ Result:

All pods = Running
👉 ✅ Infra looks fine
👉 ❌ Problem is deeper (app/identity)

✅ Step 2: Check Application Logs
kubectl logs <pod-name>
🔴 Found error:
Failed to get token from MSI endpoint
Status: 403 Forbidden

👉 ✅ Now we know:
Identity or permission issue

✅ Step 3: Verify AKS Identity Still Exists
az aks show \  --name <cluster-name> \  --resource-group <rg>
✔️ Check:
JSON"identity": {  "type":Show more lines
👉 ✅ Identity exists
👉 ❌ But maybe permissions lost

✅ Step 4: Check Role Assignments
az role assignment list \  --assignee <principal-id>
🔴 Found issue:

Missing role:
Storage Blob Data Contributor



👉 🚨 This is common after upgrade or infra changes

✅ Step 5: Re-Validate from Inside Pod
Run:
Shellkubectl exec -it <pod> -- curl http://169.254.169.254/metadata/identity/oauth2/token \  -H "Metadata:true"Show more lines
✔️ Expected:

Token returned

🔴 Actual:

Error / no token

👉 ✅ Identity endpoint issue confirmed

✅ Step 6: Check CSI / Identity Components
kubectl get pods -n kube-system
Look for:

csi-azure
aad-pod-identity (if used)
workload-identity pods

🔴 Found:

One pod in:
CrashLoopBackOff

👉 ✅ Root cause deepens:
Cluster components slightly misbehaving after upgrade

✅ Step 7: Check Node Upgrade Behavior
Shellkubectl get nodes -o wide``Show more lines
✔️ Confirm:

All nodes are 1.29
No old nodes

👉 ✅ Upgrade complete
But:
👉 ❌ Some DaemonSets not stabilized

✅ Step 8: Fix the Problem
✅ Fix 1: Re-assign Role
az role assignment create \  --assignee <principal-id> \  --role "Storage Blob Data Contributor"

✅ Fix 2: Restart Pods
Shellkubectl delete pod <pod-name>``Show more lines
👉 Forces:

New token
Fresh identity binding


✅ Fix 3: Restart CSI / Identity Pods
Shellkubectl rollout restart daemonset <csi-driver> -n kube-systemShow more lines

✅ Step 9: Validate Again
🔁 Check logs:
Shellkubectl logs <pod>Show more lines
✔️ Now:
Token acquired successfully
Connected to storage


🔁 Functional test:
Shellcurl https://app-url/healthShow more lines
✔️ 200 OK ✅

🎯 Final Root Cause Summary
👉 After AKS upgrade:

Node rotation happened ✅
System identity remained ✅
❌ Role assignment missing OR token refresh issue
❌ CSI / identity component needed restart


